// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
// Replaces Qt's file of this name, whose CMake snippet can only name a module of the Qt6 package.

//! [using the c++ api]
    Using the module's C++ API requires linking against its library, either
    directly or through other dependencies.
//! [using the c++ api]

//! [building with cmake]
    Use the \c {find_package()} command to locate the library, and link your
    target against it:

    \code
    find_package(\1 REQUIRED COMPONENTS \2)
    target_link_libraries(mytarget PRIVATE \3)
    \endcode

    The \c KF6 package is found through extra-cmake-modules: first call
    \c {find_package(ECM REQUIRED NO_MODULE)} and add \c {ECM_MODULE_PATH} to
    \c {CMAKE_MODULE_PATH}.
//! [building with cmake]

//! [building with cmake nomodule]
    Use the \c {find_package()} command to locate the library, and link your
    target against it:

    \code
    find_package(\1 REQUIRED)
    target_link_libraries(mytarget PRIVATE \2)
    \endcode
//! [building with cmake nomodule]
